# Keep .mjs checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Vite's transform fails on a CRLF .mjs that is imported from a .ts test:
#   SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token
# Plain `node --check` and a direct `import()` both parse the same file
# happily, so this only surfaces through the test pipeline. On Windows,
# core.autocrlf rewrites the file at checkout, which means a fresh clone would
# fail tests/unit/account-classification.test.ts while the committed bytes are
# perfectly valid. Pinning eol=lf removes the whole class.
*.mjs text eol=lf
